    {
      "text": "Whosoever therefore shall be ashamed of me, Mark 8:38. counted worthy to suffer shame for his name, Acts 5:41. I am not ashamed of the gospel of Christ, Rom. 1:16. I write not these things to shame you, 1 Cor. 4:14. I speak to your shame, 1 Cor. 6:5 (15:34). shame for a woman to be shorn, 1 Cor. 11:6. man have long hair, it is a shame unto him, 1 Cor. 11:14. despise ye the church of God, and shame them, 1 Cor. 11:22. it is a shame for women to speak in the church, 1 Cor. 14:35. shame even to speak of those things, Eph. 5:12. whose glory is in their shame, Philip. 3:19. Be not thou therefore ashamed of the testimony, 2 Tim. 1:8. fall away … put him to an open shame, Heb. 6:6 (D&C 76:35). Jesus … endured the cross, despising the shame, Heb. 12:2.",
